canonicalModule -- computes the canonical module of a module $M$ or an ideal $I$.
*********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        canonicalModule M
        canonicalModule I
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module over the polynomial
        ring $S=K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, with $K$ a field or an ideal $I\subset S$
  * Outputs:
      * K, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the canonical module

Description
===========

Let $S=K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$ be a polynomial ring. Given a $S$-module $M$ (or an
ideal $I\subset S$), it returns the canonical module $\omega(M)$ (or
$\omega(S/I)$), as $\mathrm{Ext}_S^{n-d}(M,S(-n))$, where $d=\dim M$ (or
$d=\dim S/I$).

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x_1..x_5];                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=(x_1^2*x_3,x_2*x_3^2*x_4,x_1*x_3^3*x_5);            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M=S^1/I;                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : canonicalModule M                                     |
|                                                           |
|o4 = subquotient ({2} | x_1^2       |, {2} | x_1^2x_3    |)|
|                  {1} | x_2x_3x_4   |  {1} | x_2x_3^2x_4 | |
|                  {0} | x_1x_3^2x_5 |  {0} | x_1x_3^3x_5 | |
|                                                           |
|                               3                           |
|o4 : S-module, subquotient of S                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note deficiencyModule: deficiencyModule, -- computes the $i$th module of
    deficiency of a module $M$ or an ideal $I$.

Ways to use canonicalModule:
============================

  * "canonicalModule(Ideal)"
  * "canonicalModule(Module)"

