deficiencyModule -- computes the $i$th module of deficiency of a module $M$ or an ideal $I$.
********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        deficiencyModule(M,i)
        deficiencyModule(I,i)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, module over the polynomial
        ring $S=K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$, with $K$ a field or an ideal $I\subset S$
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the ith module of deficiency
        of $M$

Description
===========

Let $S=K[x_1,\ldots,x_n]$ be the polynomial ring. Given a $S$-module $M$ (or an
ideal $I\subset S$), it returns the $i$th module of deficiency $\omega^i(M)$
(or $\omega^i(S/I)$), defined as $\mathrm{Ext}_S^{n-i}(M,S(-n))$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S=QQ[x_1..x_5];                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I=(x_1^2*x_3,x_2*x_3^2*x_4,x_1*x_3^3*x_5);                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M=S^1/I;                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : deficiencyModule(M,3)                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = subquotient ({-1} | -x_1   0      x_2x_4 |, {-1} | -x_2x_3x_4 x_1^2     |
|                  {-1} | 0      x_1    x_3x_5 |  {-1} | -x_3^2x_5  0         |
|                  {-2} | x_3x_5 x_2x_4 0      |  {-2} | 0          -x_1x_3x_5|
|                                                                             |
|                               3                                             |
|o4 : S-module, subquotient of S                                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|0      |)                                                                    |
|x_1    |                                                                     |
|x_2x_4 |                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note canonicalModule: canonicalModule, -- computes the canonical module of
    a module $M$ or an ideal $I$.
  * *note isSCM: isSCM, -- checks whether a module or an ideal is sequentially
    Cohen-Macaulay

